A||||10||Carrolles||Awesome Turbo||||1||
Z||000000||Carrolles||08-07-2000||06:04 PM||||This is Fiero related only in that I own a Fiero.  My nieghbor is a mechanic for a local Mazda dealership and is the president of the Miata club.  He is always trying to talk me into getting a Miata to either supplement or replace my Fiero.  Saturday he had a guy from the club over to his house.  He was driving a 93 Miata with a $5400.00 Turbo system running 14 to 16 psi boost.  It is intercooled and has a programable computer on the dash to make on the fly adjustments.  He took me for a ride and it was unbelievable what the little four banger can do with 16psi boost.  He says that when it gets dialed in it should be putting out around 240hp at the crank.<P>I was impressed!!!<P>I still like my Fiero more even if it is only a relatively stock 2.8. ||||reg||1
Z||000001||stimpy||08-07-2000||07:21 PM||||The Miata uses the same engine I have in my 323 GTX. Factory turbo and intercooled, that little 16v 1.6l puts out similar numbers to my Fiero GT. And runs as smooth as a sewing machine. I can only imagine what it would do in a lightweight aerodynamic car!  Too bad my Mazda is as ugly as a turd!||||reg||1
Z||000002||Pontiaddict||08-07-2000||08:21 PM||||For $5400.00, I'd swap a Northstar and throw 2 turbos on that. It's supposed to put out something like 600 hp.<P>It'd be a pain to fit everything in the car though.||||reg||1
Z||000003||88formula||08-07-2000||09:28 PM||||You can put a custom turbo on your 2.8 for under $4000. Design One sells them as a kit complete with everything needed to do the job.||||reg||1
Z||000004||turbo86se||08-07-2000||11:42 PM||||You said it 88Formula, every last bolt is included. Although mine was installed by IRM in Rockville, I haven't heard any complaints. Very good and reliable kit. I love having the turbo. Lots of times when I fill her up at the gas station, someone will approach me with comments on how my Fiero looks. The look on their face when I open the decklid is priceless!<P>Before Fieros, I was obsessed with Miatas. My old roommate and best friend, Scott, had a Millen Miata. I loved that car, in fact, Scott turned me on to Fieros. I was looking for a low-priced sports car to have fun with, since I couldn't afford a Miata. Scott, who now races for Porsche, said the Fieros are tough little cars with endless possibilities. I had no idea I would develop such a strong affection with the car. Now, whenever I'm driving, that's all I'm looking for! What Miata?  ||||reg||1
Z||000005||loafer87gt||08-08-2000||01:15 AM||||$5400 for a twin turbo intercooled Northstar! Not flaming you, but I think your way to low on your price, unless you plan on custom fabricating everything on your own and doing your own install. Last time I checked with Design one, they said it would be $5000 bucks for the conversion kit, $4-5000 for the motor and transmission, and an extra $6,000 for the twin turbo and intercooler. Your right about the horsepower numbers though, I heard it was supposed to be around 550 HP, that would be sweet indeed.||||reg||1
Z||000006||BBBAD GT||08-08-2000||09:30 AM||||All this talk about high high HP Fieros, I wonder how the chassis could ever handle it (I'm talking over like 350 HP).  The V8 Fiero I'm getting this weekend had a hot 350 in it (prob around 400 HP), but now it basically has a stock longblock with OK intake and carb (prob around 220-250 HP).  The owner is sooooo much more happy with the car now than before, just because of the fact that the chassis can handle it way much better.  There's also got to be a point to where the chassis starts to flex from all that torque without any braces/bars.  <P>Maybe this should be a seperate topic, but I just wanted to throw this out.  <P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://scribers.midwest.net/bbbad50/BBBAD_GT_SIG.gif">  <P><A HREF="http://scribers.midwest.net/bbbad50/Fiero.htm" TARGET=_blank>BBBAD GT</A><BR><A HREF="http://scribers.midwest.net/bbbad50/" TARGET=_blank>BBBAD 5.0</A>||||reg||1
Z||000007||1FST2M6||08-08-2000||01:59 PM||||I know at 300+lbft of torque the tires ok the whole rear suspension will fold forward about an inch. even with poly-bushings and will cut the bushings... (only a 40hp shot of NOS)  ||||reg||1
Z||000008||HYPTNOTiSE||08-09-2000||01:23 AM||||yeah i'm in the midst of doing my 3.2 rebuild. I'm going to be running 1 poly motor mount, 1 poly dogbone mount, one solid motor mount, and 2 solid trany mounts, my cradle mounts are aluminum. I think i'm going to have to box my control arms, steve hamm is working on frame connectors at the moment, i'd like to get those too.  He's making 322hp at the crank with 10psi and improber tuning. He said he just boils 245/50/16's goodyear GS-C's through 1st, spins most of the way through second, doesn't really get traction untill 3rd gear. i asked where he dumps the clutch, and he said thats tryin to slip it!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  Pretty bad ass. i think he's somewhere around 350-370Tq at the wheels.<P>------------------<BR>       Mike LeCompte<BR>86 Fiero GT 3.2L w/ Nitrous<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.tcac.net/~daddyg/hypsig.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000009||terryk||08-09-2000||11:55 AM||||During testing of the Citation X-11 (the Fiero cradle is similar but not identical), Heinracy found out that the cradle would actually warp on hard acceleration. If you look, you will see braces added to the corners of the cradle and from the cradle to the rack. John said those are an aboslute must on any cradle if you plan on really adding more torque. ||||reg||1
Z||000010||Dan86gt3.8||08-10-2000||12:14 PM||||ya I would think you would want to weld in something alot more sturdy on the front 2 cradle mounts or the two that let the cradle swing down.  If I rember right thats only like a 1/4 inch thick piece of metalwith a somewhat small bolt in it.   ||||reg||1
